  "verbalization": "Allylestrenol is linked to Pgr through a series of molecular relationships that involve progestins and steroid compounds. The evidence suggests that Allylestrenol, which resembles Gestodene and Norgestimate, binds to Pgr through a shared pathway involving progestins. This is supported by the lowest common ancestors of Allylestrenol with Gestodene and Norgestimate, both of which are progestins, and the binding of Norelgestromin to Pgr. The similarity between Allylestrenol and Gestodene, along with the binding of Norelgestromin to Pgr, indicates a potential mechanism where structurally similar compounds can interact with the same target. The recurring evidence points to a dependency on progestins and steroid compounds, suggesting that Allylestrenol may act through a similar mechanism as other progestins, thereby supporting a relationship between Allylestrenol and Pgr.",
